#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Primitives {#primitives}"
msgstr "Primitif {#primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All physical systems, whether classical or quantum, can exist in different states. For example, a car on a road can have a certain mass, position, speed, or acceleration that characterize its state. Similarly, quantum systems can also have different configurations or states, but they differ from classical systems in how we deal with measurements and state evolution. This leads to unique properties such as *superposition* and *entanglement* that are exclusive to quantum mechanics. Just like we can describe a car's state using physical properties like speed or acceleration, we can also describe the state of a quantum system using *observables*, which are mathematical objects.\n"
msgstr "Semua sistem fizikal, sama ada klasik atau kuantum, boleh wujud dalam pelbagai keadaan. Sebagai contoh, sebuah kereta di jalan raya boleh mempunyai jisim, kedudukan, kelajuan, atau pecutan tertentu yang mencirikan keadaannya. Begitu juga, sistem kuantum juga boleh mempunyai pelbagai konfigurasi atau keadaan, tetapi ia berbeza daripada sistem klasik dari segi cara kita mengendalikan pengukuran dan evolusi keadaan. Ini membawa kepada sifat unik seperti *superposisi* dan *keterikatan* yang eksklusif kepada mekanik kuantum. Sama seperti kita boleh menerangkan keadaan kereta menggunakan sifat fizikal seperti kelajuan atau pecutan, kita juga boleh menerangkan keadaan sistem kuantum menggunakan *boleh cerapan* (observables), yang merupakan objek matematik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In quantum mechanics, states are represented by normalized complex column vectors, or *kets* ($|\\psi\\rangle$), and observables are Hermitian linear operators ($\\hat{H}=\\hat{H}^{\\dagger}$) that act on the kets. An eigenvector ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) of an observable is known as an *eigenstate*. Measuring an observable for one of its eigenstates ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) will give us the corresponding eigenvalue ($\\lambda$) as readout.\n"
msgstr "Dalam mekanik kuantum, keadaan diwakili oleh vektor lajur kompleks yang ternormal, atau *ket* ($|\\psi\\rangle$), dan boleh cerapan adalah pengoperasi linear Hermitian ($\\hat{H}=\\hat{H}^{\\dagger}$) yang bertindak ke atas ket. Vektor eigen ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) bagi sesuatu boleh cerapan dikenali sebagai *eigenstate*. Mengukur sesuatu boleh cerapan untuk salah satu eigenstatenya ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) akan menghasilkan nilai eigen ($\\lambda$) yang sepadan sebagai bacaan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you're wondering how to measure a quantum system and what you can measure, Qiskit offers two <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Basic and fundamental operations or data type. Qiskit has the Sampler and Estimator primitives to serve as building blocks to easily construct complex algorithmic workloads.\">primitives</DefinitionTooltip> that can help:\n"
msgstr "Jika anda tertanya-tanya cara mengukur sistem kuantum dan apa yang boleh diukur, Qiskit menawarkan dua <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Operasi asas dan fundamental atau jenis data. Qiskit mempunyai primitif Sampler dan Estimator yang berfungsi sebagai blok binaan untuk membina beban kerja algoritma yang kompleks dengan mudah.\">primitif</DefinitionTooltip> yang boleh membantu:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Sampler`: Given a quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$, this primitive obtains the probability of each possible computational basis state.\n"
msgstr "`Sampler`: Diberi keadaan kuantum $|\\psi\\rangle$, primitif ini mendapatkan kebarangkalian setiap keadaan asas pengiraan yang mungkin.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Estimator`: Given a quantum observable $\\hat{H}$ and a state $|\\psi\\rangle$, this primitive computes the expected value of $\\hat{H}$.\n"
msgstr "`Estimator`: Diberi boleh cerapan kuantum $\\hat{H}$ dan keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle$, primitif ini mengira nilai jangkaan $\\hat{H}$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Sampler primitive {#the-sampler-primitive}"
msgstr "Primitif Sampler {#the-sampler-primitive}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Sampler` primitive calculates the probability of obtaining each possible state $|k\\rangle$ from the computational basis, given a quantum circuit that prepares the state $|\\psi\\rangle$. It calculates\n"
msgstr "Primitif `Sampler` mengira kebarangkalian mendapatkan setiap keadaan yang mungkin $|k\\rangle$ daripada asas pengiraan, diberi litar kuantum yang menyediakan keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle$. Ia mengira\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p_k = |\\langle k | \\psi \\rangle|^2 \\quad \\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,2^n-1\\},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p_k = |\\langle k | \\psi \\rangle|^2 \\quad \\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,2^n-1\\},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where $n$ is the number of qubits, and $k$ the integer representation of any possible output binary string $\\{0,1\\}^n$ (that is, integers base $2$).\n"
msgstr "Di mana $n$ adalah bilangan qubit, dan $k$ ialah perwakilan integer bagi mana-mana rentetan binari output yang mungkin $\\{0,1\\}^n$ (iaitu, integer asas $2$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IBM Quantum [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) runs the circuit multiple times on a quantum device, performing measurements on each run, and reconstructing the probability distribution from the recovered bitstrings. The more runs (or *shots*) it performs, the more accurate the results will be, but this requires more time and quantum resources.\n"
msgstr "IBM Quantum [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) menjalankan litar beberapa kali pada peranti kuantum, melakukan pengukuran pada setiap jalankan, dan membina semula taburan kebarangkalian daripada rentetan bit yang diperoleh. Lebih banyak jalankan (atau *shots*) yang dilakukan, semakin tepat hasilnya, tetapi ini memerlukan lebih banyak masa dan sumber kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, since the number of possible outputs grows exponentially with the number of qubits $n$ (that is, $2^n$), the number of shots will need to grow exponentially as well in order to capture a _dense_ probability distribution. Therefore, `Sampler` is only efficient for *sparse* probability distributions; where the target state $|\\psi\\rangle$ must be expressible as a linear combination of the computational basis states, with the number of terms growing at most polynomially with the number of qubits:\n"
msgstr "Walau bagaimanapun, oleh kerana bilangan output yang mungkin meningkat secara eksponen dengan bilangan qubit $n$ (iaitu, $2^n$), bilangan shots juga perlu meningkat secara eksponen bagi menangkap taburan kebarangkalian yang _padat_. Oleh itu, `Sampler` hanya cekap untuk taburan kebarangkalian yang *jarang*; di mana keadaan sasaran $|\\psi\\rangle$ mestilah boleh dinyatakan sebagai gabungan linear bagi keadaan asas pengiraan, dengan bilangan sebutan yang meningkat paling banyak secara polinomial dengan bilangan qubit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k |k\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k |k\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Sampler` can also be configured to retrieve probabilities from a subsection of the circuit, representing a subset of the total possible states.\n"
msgstr "`Sampler` juga boleh dikonfigurasi untuk mendapatkan kebarangkalian daripada bahagian litar, yang mewakili subset bagi semua keadaan yang mungkin.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Estimator primitive {#the-estimator-primitive}"
msgstr "Primitif Estimator {#the-estimator-primitive}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Estimator` primitive calculates the expectation value of an observable $\\hat{H}$ for a quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$; where the observable probabilities can be expressed as $p_\\lambda = |\\langle\\lambda|\\psi\\rangle|^2$, being $|\\lambda\\rangle$ the eigenstates of the observable $\\hat{H}$. The expectation value is then defined as the average of all possible outcomes $\\lambda$ (that is, the eigenvalues of the observable) of a measurement of the state $|\\psi\\rangle$, weighted by the corresponding probabilities:\n"
msgstr "Primitif `Estimator` mengira nilai jangkaan bagi boleh cerapan $\\hat{H}$ untuk keadaan kuantum $|\\psi\\rangle$; di mana kebarangkalian boleh cerapan boleh dinyatakan sebagai $p_\\lambda = |\\langle\\lambda|\\psi\\rangle|^2$, dengan $|\\lambda\\rangle$ ialah eigenstate bagi boleh cerapan $\\hat{H}$. Nilai jangkaan kemudiannya ditakrifkan sebagai purata semua hasil yang mungkin $\\lambda$ (iaitu, nilai eigen bagi boleh cerapan) bagi pengukuran keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle$, berpemberat dengan kebarangkalian yang sepadan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi := \\sum_\\lambda p_\\lambda \\lambda = \\langle \\psi | \\hat{H} | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi := \\sum_\\lambda p_\\lambda \\lambda = \\langle \\psi | \\hat{H} | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, calculating the expectation value of an observable is not always possible, as we often don't know its eigenbasis. The IBM Quantum [`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) uses a complex algebraic process to estimate the expectation value on a real quantum device by breaking down the observable into a combination of other observables whose eigenbasis we do know.\n"
msgstr "Walau bagaimanapun, mengira nilai jangkaan sesuatu boleh cerapan tidak selalunya boleh dilakukan, kerana kita sering tidak tahu asas eigennya. IBM Quantum [`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) menggunakan proses algebra yang kompleks untuk menganggar nilai jangkaan pada peranti kuantum sebenar dengan menguraikan boleh cerapan tersebut kepada gabungan boleh cerapan lain yang asas eigennya kita sudah ketahui.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In simpler terms, `Estimator` breaks down any observable that it doesn't know how to measure into simpler, measurable observables called <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Set of matrices commonly used in quantum computing to represent and manipulate quantum states, consisting of the identity matrix and the three Pauli matrices (X, Y, and Z).\">Pauli operators</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
"Any operator can be expressed as a combination of $4^n$ Pauli operators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara lebih mudah, `Estimator` menguraikan mana-mana boleh cerapan yang tidak tahu cara mengukurnya kepada boleh cerapan yang lebih mudah dan boleh diukur yang dipanggil <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Set matriks yang biasa digunakan dalam pengkomputeran kuantum untuk mewakili dan memanipulasi keadaan kuantum, terdiri daripada matriks identiti dan tiga matriks Pauli (X, Y, dan Z).\">pengoperasi Pauli</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
"Mana-mana pengoperasi boleh dinyatakan sebagai gabungan $4^n$ pengoperasi Pauli.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{P}_k :=\n"
"\\sigma_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\sigma_{k_0} \\quad\n"
"\\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,4^n-1\\}, \\\\\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{P}_k :=\n"
"\\sigma_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\sigma_{k_0} \\quad\n"
"\\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,4^n-1\\}, \\\\\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "such that\n"
msgstr "sedemikian\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum^{4^n-1}_{k=0} w_k \\hat{P}_k\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum^{4^n-1}_{k=0} w_k \\hat{P}_k\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $n$ is the number of qubits, $k \\equiv k_{n-1} \\cdots k_0$ for $k_l \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4 \\equiv \\{0, 1, 2, 3\\}$ (that is, integers base $4$), and $(\\sigma_0, \\sigma_1, \\sigma_2, \\sigma_3) := (I, X, Y, Z)$.\n"
msgstr "di mana $n$ adalah bilangan qubit, $k \\equiv k_{n-1} \\cdots k_0$ untuk $k_l \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4 \\equiv \\{0, 1, 2, 3\\}$ (iaitu, integer asas $4$), dan $(\\sigma_0, \\sigma_1, \\sigma_2, \\sigma_3) := (I, X, Y, Z)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After performing this decomposition, `Estimator` derives a new circuit $V_k|\\psi\\rangle$ for each observable $\\hat{P}_k$ (from the original circuit), to effectively *diagonalize* the Pauli observable in the computational basis and measure it. We can easily measure Pauli observables because we know $V_k$ ahead of time, which is not the case generally for other observables.\n"
msgstr "Selepas melakukan penguraian ini, `Estimator` menghasilkan litar baru $V_k|\\psi\\rangle$ untuk setiap boleh cerapan $\\hat{P}_k$ (daripada litar asal), untuk secara efektif *mendiagonalkan* boleh cerapan Pauli dalam asas pengiraan dan mengukurnya. Kita boleh mengukur boleh cerapan Pauli dengan mudah kerana kita tahu $V_k$ lebih awal, yang tidak berlaku secara umum untuk boleh cerapan lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each $\\hat{P}_{k}$, the `Estimator` runs the corresponding circuit on a quantum device multiple times, measures the output state in the computational basis, and calculates the probability $p_{kj}$ of obtaining each possible output $j$. It then looks for the eigenvalue $\\lambda_{kj}$ of $P_k$ corresponding to each output $j$, multiplies by $w_k$, and adds all the results together to obtain the expected value of the observable $\\hat{H}$ for the given state $|\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Untuk setiap $\\hat{P}_{k}$, `Estimator` menjalankan litar yang sepadan pada peranti kuantum beberapa kali, mengukur keadaan output dalam asas pengiraan, dan mengira kebarangkalian $p_{kj}$ untuk mendapatkan setiap output yang mungkin $j$. Ia kemudian mencari nilai eigen $\\lambda_{kj}$ bagi $P_k$ yang sepadan dengan setiap output $j$, darabkan dengan $w_k$, dan tambah semua hasilnya untuk mendapatkan nilai jangkaan boleh cerapan $\\hat{H}$ bagi keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle$ yang diberikan.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj},\n"
"$$\n"
"Since calculating the expectation value of $4^n$ Paulis is impractical (that is, exponentially growing), `Estimator` can only be efficient when a large amount of $w_k$ are zero (that is, *sparse* Pauli decomposition instead of *dense*). Formally we say that, for this computation to be *efficiently solvable*, the number of non-zero terms has to grow at most polynomially with the number of qubits $n$: $\\hat{H} = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k \\hat{P}_k$.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj},\n"
"$$\n"
"Oleh kerana mengira nilai jangkaan $4^n$ Pauli adalah tidak praktikal (iaitu, pertumbuhan eksponen), `Estimator` hanya boleh cekap apabila banyak $w_k$ adalah sifar (iaitu, penguraian Pauli yang *jarang* berbanding *padat*). Secara formal kita katakan bahawa, agar pengiraan ini *boleh diselesaikan dengan cekap*, bilangan sebutan bukan sifar mestilah meningkat paling banyak secara polinomial dengan bilangan qubit $n$: $\\hat{H} = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k \\hat{P}_k.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reader may notice the implicit assumption that probability <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The process of taking several measurements of one or several things.\">sampling</DefinitionTooltip> also needs to be efficient as explained for `Sampler`, which means\n"
msgstr "Pembaca mungkin perasan andaian tersirat bahawa <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Proses mengambil beberapa pengukuran ke atas satu atau beberapa perkara.\">pensampelan</DefinitionTooltip> kebarangkalian juga perlu cekap seperti yang dijelaskan untuk `Sampler`, yang bermaksud\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k}^{\\text{Poly}(n)} w_k \\sum_{j}^{\\text{Poly}(n)}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k}^{\\text{Poly}(n)} w_k \\sum_{j}^{\\text{Poly}(n)}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Guided example to calculate expectation values {#guided-example-to-calculate-expectation-values}"
msgstr "Contoh berpandu untuk mengira nilai jangkaan {#guided-example-to-calculate-expectation-values}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's assume the single-qubit state $|+\\rangle := H|0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle)$, and observable\n"
msgstr "Mari kita andaikan keadaan satu qubit $|+\\rangle := H|0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle)$, dan boleh cerapan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\hat{H}\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"-1 & 2 \\\\\n"
"2 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = 2X - Z\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\hat{H}\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"-1 & 2 \\\\\n"
"2 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = 2X - Z\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with the following theoretical expectation value $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = \\langle+|\\hat{H}|+\\rangle = 2$.\n"
msgstr "dengan nilai jangkaan teori berikut $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = \\langle+|\\hat{H}|+\\rangle = 2$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since we do not know how to measure this observable, we cannot compute its expectation value directly, and we need to re-express it as $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = 2\\langle X \\rangle_+ - \\langle Z \\rangle_+ $. Which can be shown to evaluate to the same result by virtue of noting that $\\langle+|X|+\\rangle = 1$, and $\\langle+|Z|+\\rangle = 0$.\n"
msgstr "Oleh kerana kita tidak tahu cara mengukur boleh cerapan ini, kita tidak boleh mengira nilai jangkaannya secara terus, dan kita perlu menyatakannya semula sebagai $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = 2\\langle X \\rangle_+ - \\langle Z \\rangle_+ $. Yang boleh ditunjukkan memberikan hasil yang sama dengan memperhatikan bahawa $\\langle+|X|+\\rangle = 1$, dan $\\langle+|Z|+\\rangle = 0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let see how to compute $\\langle X \\rangle_+$ and $\\langle Z \\rangle_+$ directly. Since $X$ and $Z$ do not commute (that is, they don't share the same eigenbasis), they cannot be measured simultaneously, therefore we need the auxiliary circuits:\n"
msgstr "Mari kita lihat cara mengira $\\langle X \\rangle_+$ dan $\\langle Z \\rangle_+$ secara terus. Oleh kerana $X$ dan $Z$ tidak bertukar (iaitu, mereka tidak berkongsi asas eigen yang sama), mereka tidak boleh diukur serentak, oleh itu kita memerlukan litar pembantu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/7c32e970-f9cb-48ec-a60b-2dccb0744141-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/7c32e970-f9cb-48ec-a60b-2dccb0744141-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/ec3cf7af-66b2-4ea9-94d7-6ec6ba2bfc5e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/ec3cf7af-66b2-4ea9-94d7-6ec6ba2bfc5e-0.avif)\n"

